        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-09T22:56:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Log space is limited by SRAM on the EC. When we actually implement this in production, we will fetch logs once and save them to persistent storage (similar to `PDLOG` entries in syslog, or EC console logs saved in /var/log) so nothing will be lost.",
      "parentUuid": "b16f4d15_d69de083",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "b8a5e66bfe3e2dc97f9aad90f6250761bf2b94c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97e713d7_a1aa3f25",
        "filename": "common/tpm_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-09T23:03:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ah, so the log is not kept in flash (sorry I missed your previous patches), I guess it is good in a way, as we don\u0027t have much room left there.\n\nbut whatever the size of the log buffer is, it could be circular, and this command could be return all stored entries in order. This would make it easier for instance when using the tpm_send extension you suggesting in the other patch, the user would not care about accidentally wiping out the log without storing it.\n\nIs this (one entry at at time) how it is done for the PD also?",
      "parentUuid": "578e69a1_570fe2d4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "b8a5e66bfe3e2dc97f9aad90f6250761bf2b94c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "711449e8_0222e814",
        "filename": "common/tpm_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-09T23:23:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, for PD logging, logs are automatically and always removed from the queue once retrieved through the host command. We can make a change here to not throw away log entries unless the queue is full. The downside is that it would make it slightly harder for the log retriever to determine whether a log entry is new or already retrieved, especially considering we\u0027re currently using relative timestamps (so timestamp matching won\u0027t work). Maybe I can add a parameter to VENDOR_CC_GET_LOG_ENTRY that selects whether to operate in \u0027pop\u0027 or \u0027get\u0027 mode?",
      "parentUuid": "97e713d7_a1aa3f25",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "b8a5e66bfe3e2dc97f9aad90f6250761bf2b94c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe65a943_7ca616ec",
        "filename": "common/tpm_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-09T23:29:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t want this to be different from PD logging if it does not have to.\n\nIf the tools for retrieving and keeping the TPM log locally on the AP are upcoming, this should be fine.",
      "parentUuid": "711449e8_0222e814",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 35,
